## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Tư: Quyết định thiết kế

Nói to bằng tiếng Anh, ghi âm:

> *"I picked optimistic locking over pessimistic locking for concurrent edits.*
> *The scenario is a user with the app open on a phone and a tablet, both editing the same meal. Without protection the second write silently overwrites the first — a lost update.*
> *Optimistic means I don't lock anything. Every row has a version number, the client sends the version it's holding, and the update only applies if the version still matches. If it doesn't, nobody wins by accident — I return 409 and the client reconciles.*
> *I chose that over SELECT FOR UPDATE for one specific reason: my clients are phones on mobile networks. A pessimistic lock would be held across network latency I don't control. If someone loses signal holding a lock, everyone else waits.*
> *The tradeoff is that the client has to handle retry, which is more work on my side. I think that's the right trade when conflicts are rare."*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `lost update` | mất cập nhật | *That's a lost update.* |
| `reconcile` (v) | hoà giải, dung hoà | *The client reconciles.* |
| `hold a lock` | giữ khoá | *A lock held across network latency.* |
| `silently overwrite` | ghi đè im lặng | *The second write silently overwrites the first.* |
| `the right trade` | đánh đổi hợp lý | *I think that's the right trade.* |

